# Build artifacts: Rust's target dir lives outside the repo (see the README),
# and the Node sidecar is a ~93 MB copy of the local node binary that belongs on
# nobody's disk - on every platform, not just the .exe one. This checkout sits
# in its build workspace, so the workspace's own target dir is ignored here too.
/target/
/desktop/src-tauri/target/
/desktop/src-tauri/gen/
/desktop/sidecar/*.exe
/desktop/sidecar/*.dll
/desktop/sidecar/node
/desktop/sidecar/node-*

# Local state - sessions, staged uploads, spilled tool output and logs are
# machine-local by design.
/.aipass/
.mimosa/

node_modules/
*.log
